but remains individual-model-level; our DIF is group-level and complementary\\\\\\\"\\\\n    abstract: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20T17:30:00.000Z\\\\\\\"\\\\n  polo2026growingpains:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Growing Pains: Extensible and Efficient LLM Benchmarking Via Fixed Parameter Calibration\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Polo, F.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv\\\\\\\"\\\\n    doi: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    bibtex_key: \\\\\\\"polo2026growingpains\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"irt_equating\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"direct-competitor\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Uses multidimensional IRT with fixed-parameter calibration and 100 anchor items for extensible evaluation (rho>=0.9); addresses score comparability but NOT contamination detection or item regeneration\\\\\\\"\\\\n    abstract: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20T17:30:00.000Z\\\\\\\"\\\\n  polo2026psnirt:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Lost in Benchmarks? Rethinking Large Language Model Benchmarking with Item Response Theory\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Polo, F.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"AAAI 2026\\\\\\\"\\\\n    doi: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    bibtex_key: \\\\\\\"polo2026psnirt\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"irt_equating\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"method-component\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"PSN-IRT analyzes benchmark quality via 4PL IRT; provides published IRT parameters for MMLU we can use in semi-synthetic validation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    abstract: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: 